# `ProtocolRuntime`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

`ProtocolRuntime` marks the built dispatch layer created by [`PreparedProtocol`](./PreparedProtocol). A runtime holds operational protocol state: dispatch tables, codecs, transport adapters, and any handles required to translate an endpoint event into component resolution under the declared scope topology.

It intentionally does not prescribe an endpoint type or endpoint loop. Implement [`Serve`](./Serve) separately for each endpoint type the runtime supports. This lets one dispatch runtime serve, for example, several RPC transports without duplicating its validation or DI integration.

The runtime's error type covers protocol dispatch and serving construction errors as defined by the implementation. Application startup, reload coordination, and final cleanup remain application lifecycle concerns.

See [the custom protocol guide](/docs/latest/framework/extensions/protocol-authoring) for serving and shutdown ownership.

